## Code Quality Standards to Always Enforce

### Laravel
- Controllers must be thin — receive request → call Service → return Inertia response
- Always use FormRequest classes for validation — never `$request->validate()` inline
- Always use API Resources for data passed to Inertia — never raw models or `->toArray()`
- Always use named routes — never hardcoded URLs
- Always use route model binding with locale-aware slugs on public routes (`{project:slug}`)
- Query logic goes in a **Repository** (implementing an interface); business logic/orchestration goes in a **Service**; Controllers call Services only
- Always use `$fillable` on models — never `$guarded = []`
- Always add database indexes on foreign keys and on `slug` + `language_id` combinations
- Always wrap multi-step DB operations in `DB::transaction()` (e.g. creating a Project + dispatching translation jobs)
- Always use `.env` for sensitive config (`DEEPL_API_KEY` etc.) — never hardcode keys
- Any new translatable model must follow the exact `{model}` + `{model}_translations` pattern already established — no exceptions or shortcuts

### Translation / Jobs
- Never call `DeepLTranslatorService` synchronously from a request — always via `TranslateContentJob`
- Every new Job must declare `$tries`, `$backoff`, and `$timeout` explicitly — no relying on defaults
- Every translation Job must update `translation_status` on success and on final failure
- Use `WithoutOverlapping` on any job keyed by a model + locale combination

### Vue / Inertia
- Always use `<script setup>` with Composition API — never Options API
- Always type props with `defineProps<{}>()` TypeScript generics
- Always use `useForm()` from `@inertiajs/vue3` for form submissions — never raw axios
- Always use `<Link>` from `@inertiajs/vue3` for internal links — never `<a href>`
- Always handle loading state on buttons during form submission (`form.processing`)
- Always display validation errors from `form.errors.fieldName`
- Always use named route helper `route('name')` via Ziggy — never hardcode URLs
- Never mutate props directly — use emits or local reactive copies
- Never use `any` type without a comment explaining why
- Always clean up event listeners/intervals in `onUnmounted()`
- Reuse shared components (`<TranslationTabs>`, `<MediaUploader>`, `<IconPicker>`, `<AppSelect>`) instead of rebuilding similar UI per page
- Always use `<AppSelect>` for dropdowns — never native `<select>` (see `system-design-rule.mdc` Dropdowns section)

### Tailwind CSS
- Always use the dark cork design tokens from the project brief (colors, spacing, radius)
- Never write custom CSS unless Tailwind truly cannot achieve it
- Never use arbitrary values like `w-[347px]` unless genuinely necessary
- Always use responsive prefixes (`sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`) for layout shifts
- Always account for `dir="rtl"` — avoid hardcoded `ml-`/`mr-`/`left-`/`right-` where a logical property (`ms-`, `me-`, `start-`, `end-`) would work correctly in both directions

