## Documentation Mode — Auto-Generated LinkedIn Posts Per Phase

Because I'm sharing this build publicly as I go, Cursor has an additional standing role: **after every completed phase** (per the Build Order in `project-brief-rule.mdc` Section 11 — Foundation, Translation Infrastructure, Public Shell, Portfolio & Services, Blog & Leads, Admin Panel Polish, SEO & Launch), Cursor must generate a full LinkedIn post documenting that phase.

### When to trigger
- At the natural end of a phase (all its steps in the Build Order are done and working), not after every individual step
- Also trigger mid-phase if something genuinely noteworthy happens — a mistake caught and fixed, a non-obvious best practice applied, a performance/SEO/security decision most developers skip. Flag it in the moment: `📸 Milestone: [why this is worth its own post]`, then generate the post once that piece of work is finished.

### What the post must contain
Write in **Egyptian Arabic (عامية مصرية)**, same voice and structure as the posts already written for this project (see the two example posts already produced in this conversation — same tone: direct, practical, a bit personal, not corporate/stiff). Each post should:

1. Open with a short recap of what this phase covers (1-2 sentences) — assume some readers are new and haven't seen earlier posts
2. Explain the **specific technical challenge or decision** tackled in this phase in real detail — not vague ("we improved performance") but concrete ("we indexed X because Y query was doing Z")
3. Highlight **at least one thing most developers get wrong or skip** in this exact area (database design, performance, SEO, security, translation/i18n, queues, etc.) — this is the core value of the post, don't skip it or make it generic
4. Explain the reasoning/trade-off behind the decision made — why this approach over the obvious/naive one
5. Mention relevant tools/patterns used in that phase (e.g. Repository/Service pattern, Spatie Media Library, DeepL job design, specific Laravel features)
6. Close with a short line previewing the next phase, and the standard sign-off (Ahmed Sanad, Software Engineer, following-the-journey framing) with hashtags — reuse the hashtag set established in the earlier posts, add 1-2 topic-specific tags relevant to that phase (e.g. `#DatabaseDesign`, `#SEO`, `#Performance`, `#Laravel`)
7. Do **not** mention LinkedIn by name inside the post itself, and do not fabricate specific numbers/metrics that weren't actually part of the work

### Where to save it
- Create a folder named exactly `LinkedInPosts` at the project root if it doesn't already exist
- Save each post as a markdown file: `LinkedInPosts/{phase-number}-{short-phase-slug}.md` — e.g. `LinkedInPosts/01-foundation.md`, `LinkedInPosts/02-translation-infrastructure.md`
- If a mid-phase milestone post is generated separately from the phase-end post, suffix it: `LinkedInPosts/02b-deepl-job-failure-handling.md`

### After generating
- Tell me the post was created and give a one-line summary of its angle/hook, don't paste the full post inline in the chat unless I ask — I'll open the file myself
- Never auto-publish anything — this only ever produces a file for me to review and post manually

